T*(  Posner, Circuit Judge.  Twelve years ago)Tj
T*(the plaintiffs filed this suit against)Tj
T*(the board of education of Rockford,)Tj
T*(Illinois, charging that the board had)Tj
T*(intentionally discriminated against black)Tj
T*(and Hispanic students. Though nominally a)Tj
T*(new suit, it was actually a continuation)Tj
T*(of school desegregation litigation that)Tj
T*(had started long before and had resulted)Tj
T*(in the entry of a remedial decree as)Tj
T*(early as 1973. See Quality Education for)Tj
T*(All Children, Inc. v. School Board, 362)Tj
T*(F. Supp. 985 \(N.D. Ill. 1973\).)Tj
T*(Realistically, we are dealing with a)Tj
T*(lawsuit that is almost 30 years old.)Tj
T*()Tj
T*(  In 1994, the district judge found, by)Tj
T*(inference from disparities in educational)Tj
T*(achievement between white and minority)Tj
T*(students and from the school board's)Tj
T*(failure to take effective measures to)Tj
T*(prevent individual public schools from)Tj
T*(becoming all white or all minority, that)Tj
T*(the board had indeed engaged in)Tj
