T*(intentional racial discrimination. 851 F.)Tj
T*(Supp. 905 \(N.D. Ill. 1994\). The board did)Tj
T*(not appeal, and so the litigation moved)Tj
T*(into the remedial stage, presided over by)Tj
T*(a magistrate judge with the consent of)Tj
T*(the parties. A formidably complex and)Tj
T*(ambitious remedial decree was entered in)Tj
T*(1996, provoking appeals that led us the)Tj
T*(following year to vacate many of its)Tj
T*(provisions, such as racial quotas for)Tj
T*(cheerleaders, superseniority for minority)Tj
T*(teachers, unrealistic goals for closing)Tj
T*(the white-minority gap in test scores,)Tj
T*(and limits on the number of minority stu)Tj
T*(dents who could enroll in remedial)Tj
T*(classes. 111 F.3d 528 \(7th Cir. 1997\). We)Tj
T*(pointedly warned against "ambitious)Tj
T*(schemes of social engineering" and stated)Tj
T*(that children "should not be made)Tj
T*(subjects of utopian projects." Id. at)Tj
T*(534. Apart from misdescribing our opinion)Tj
T*(as having merely "modified" certain)Tj
T*(provisions of the decree, the magistrate)Tj
T*(judge managed to avoid any reference to)Tj
T*(that opinion in his latest, 57-page)Tj
T*(opinion here under review.)Tj
T*()Tj
T*(  Later we remarked "the failure of the)Tj
T*(parties, and, it seems, the magistrate)Tj
T*(judge and the special master who is)Tj
T*(assisting him, to heed the admonition of)Tj
T*(the Supreme Court, see Missouri v.)Tj
T*(Jenkins, 515 U.S. 70, 99 \(1995\); Board of)Tj
T*(Education v. Dowell, 498 U.S. 237, 248)Tj
T*(\(1991\), which we have repeated, United)Tj
T*(States v. Board of School Commissioners,)Tj
T*(128 F.3d 507, 510 \(7th Cir. 1997\), to)Tj
T*(bend every effort to winding up school)Tj
T*(litigation and returning the operation of)Tj
T*(the schools to the local school)Tj
T*(authorities." 153 F.3d 834 \(7th Cir.)Tj
T*(1998\) \(per curiam\). And the following)Tj
T*(year, in still another opinion, we warned)Tj
T*(of "the looming interminability of this)Tj
T*(litigation," and noting the school)Tj
T*(board's representation that full)Tj
T*(compliance with the decree was achievable)Tj
T*(by 2002 we suggested that the board)Tj
T*(submit to the magistrate judge a plan for)Tj
T*(winding up the litigation. 171 F.3d 1083,)Tj
T*(1090-91 \(7th Cir. 1999\). The board then)Tj
T*(moved the magistrate judge to dissolve)Tj
T*(the decree, effective June 30, 2002, the)Tj
T*(end of the 2001 school year. The board)Tj
T*(argued that it had achieved full)Tj
T*(compliance with the decree's objectives)Tj
T*(and that the remaining inequalities in)Tj
T*(educational achievement between white and)Tj
T*(minority students could not be attributed)Tj
T*(to the illegal conduct on which the)Tj
