T*(litigation was based. \(Why the board)Tj
T*(asked for deferred rather than immediate)Tj
T*(dissolution is unclear, but we are not)Tj
T*(disposed to give it more relief than it)Tj
T*(asked for.\) The magistrate judge agreed)Tj
T*(to relax some provisions of the decree,)Tj
T*(but ruled that others must continue for)Tj
T*(at least another six \(now five\) years.)Tj
T*(The plaintiffs would like the decree to)Tj
T*(continue in effect for at least 11 more)Tj
T*(years. We stress "at least." Nothing in)Tj
T*(the logic of either the magistrate)Tj
T*(judge's opinion or the plaintiffs' brief)Tj
T*(on appeal suggests any natural terminus)Tj
T*(to the decree.)Tj
T*()Tj
T*(  Through the end of 1999 the taxpayers of)Tj
T*(Rockford had incurred total costs of $238)Tj
T*(million to comply with the 1996 decree)Tj
T*(and its predecessors going back only to)Tj
T*(1989, of which more than half had been)Tj
T*(incurred since 1996. By now the total)Tj
T*(must be substantially greater. Attorneys')Tj
T*(fees alone are approaching $20 million.)Tj
T*(Twenty percent of the school district)Tj
T*(property taxes paid by homeowners in)Tj
T*(Rockford go to fund the decree. As a)Tj
T*(result of the improvements enabled by)Tj
T*(this large expenditure, and a policy of)Tj
T*(allowing parents to choose which Rockford)Tj
T*(public school to send their kids to, the)Tj
T*(school district had by the end of 1999,)Tj
T*(when the school board filed its motion to)Tj
T*(dissolve the decree, succeeded in)Tj
T*(desegregating its schools. Desegregation)Tj
T*(had been defined by the magistrate judge)Tj
T*(as the condition in which the minority)Tj
T*(composition of each school would not)Tj
T*(deviate by more than 15 percentage points)Tj
T*(from the minority composition of the)Tj
T*(population of the school district.)Tj
T*(Because this is a tighter range than)Tj
T*(imposed in most school desegregation)Tj
T*(cases, the Rockford public schools are)Tj
T*(now less segregated than those in any)Tj
T*(previous case in which a school system)Tj
T*(was declared "unitary" \(that is, declared)Tj
T*(sufficiently desegregated to require the)Tj
T*(dissolution of the decree and the return)Tj
T*(of control of the public schools to the)Tj
T*(school board\). The plaintiffs fear)Tj
T*(backsliding, and so want a wait-and-see)Tj
T*(period of at least 15 years after)Tj
T*(desegregation, during which the decree)Tj
T*(would remain in force.)Tj
T*()Tj
T*(  The length of the litigation, the scale)Tj
T*(of the expenditures, and the achievement)Tj
T*(of desegregation constitute, against the)Tj
T*(background of applicable law, compelling)Tj
