T*(which it is not responsible. Insofar as)Tj
T*(the factors that we have mentioned,)Tj
T*(rather than unlawful conduct by the)Tj
T*(Rockford school board in years past, are)Tj
T*(responsible for lags in educational)Tj
T*(achievement by minority students, the)Tj
T*(board has no duty that a federal court)Tj
T*(can enforce to help those students catch)Tj
T*(up. It may have a moral duty; it has no)Tj
T*(federal constitutional duty.)Tj
T*()Tj
T*(  No effort has been made by the)Tj
T*(plaintiffs, despite our warnings, to)Tj
T*(partition, however crudely, the lag in)Tj
T*(achievement that is due to the school)Tj
T*(board's past illegalities and the lag)Tj
T*(that is due to other factors, factors for)Tj
T*(which the school board bears no federal)Tj
T*(legal responsibility. The partition could)Tj
T*(be made by comparing minority academic)Tj
T*(performance in Rockford with the)Tj
T*(performance of minority students in other)Tj
T*(school districts after adjusting for the)Tj
T*(various factors that are not the school)Tj
T*(board's legal responsibility yet might be)Tj
T*(thought to influence the academic)Tj
T*(performance of Rockford's minority)Tj
T*(students, such as poverty, family)Tj
T*(stability, health, class size, and)Tj
T*(quality of teachers. There are)Tj
T*(statistical methods for holding these)Tj
T*(factors constant in order to isolate the)Tj
T*(influence, if any, of the board's illegal)Tj
T*(conduct on the academic performance of)Tj
T*(Rockford's minority students. No such)Tj
T*(scientific comparison has been attempted-)Tj
T*(-nor even anything cruder.)Tj
T*()Tj
T*(  The plaintiffs' failure to recognize the)Tj
T*(importance of trying to unpack the causes)Tj
T*(of disparate educational performance is)Tj
T*(illustrated by their contention that)Tj
T*(although the Rockford schools may now be)Tj
T*(desegregated, the classrooms within those)Tj
T*(schools remain segregated and until they)Tj
T*(are desegregrated the decree must remain)Tj
T*(in force. What they mean by the)Tj
T*(classrooms still being segregated is that)Tj
T*(minority students are underrepresented in)Tj
T*(advanced courses. Yet enrollment in those)Tj
T*(courses is open. No one is being kept)Tj
T*(out. \(If enrollment were not open but)Tj
T*(instead were rationed by test scores, a)Tj
T*(much smaller percentage of minority)Tj
T*(students would be enrolled in the)Tj
T*(advanced classes, the magistrate judge)Tj
T*(found--6 percent rather than 23 percent.\))Tj
T*(To suppose that minority students are)Tj
T*(enrolling in these classes at a lower)Tj
T*(rate than white students because of)Tj
