T*(school segregation in the past is)Tj
T*(illogical, or at least unsubstantiated.)Tj
T*(The schools are desegregated, the)Tj
T*(advanced courses are open to any student,)Tj
T*(and if fewer minority students are)Tj
T*(enrolling than their proportion in the)Tj
T*(school or school district as a whole, the)Tj
T*(natural inference is not that the)Tj
T*(proportion is being held down by the fact)Tj
T*(that years ago the schools were)Tj
T*(segregated. That is conceivable, but so)Tj
T*(improbable that evidence is required to)Tj
T*(use the fact as a basis for continuing a)Tj
T*(federal judicial officer in control of)Tj
T*(the public school system. The plaintiffs')Tj
T*(case is an extreme version of post hoc)Tj
T*(ergo propter hoc. It is provincial and)Tj
T*(naive to suppose that because Rockford)Tj
T*(once engaged in de facto segregation of)Tj
T*(its public schools, the choices of its)Tj
T*(minority students regarding voluntary)Tj
T*(enrollment in advanced classes open to)Tj
T*(all are a legacy of that segregation.)Tj
