T*(latter form of compliance does not)Tj
T*(exploit loopholes and ambiguities.)Tj
T*(Philips Medical Systems Int'l B.V. v.)Tj
T*(Bruetman, 8 F.3d 600, 604 \(7th Cir.)Tj
T*(1993\); United States v. Board of)Tj
T*(Education, 799 F.2d 281, 289-90, 295 \(7th)Tj
T*(Cir. 1986\); Manning v. School Board, No.)Tj
T*(99-2049, 2001 WL 264977, at *16 \(11th)Tj
T*(Cir. March 16, 2001\). It is not, as the)Tj
T*(plaintiffs would have it, that the school)Tj
T*(board must "actively" support the decree,)Tj
T*(must express "commitment" to it, and,)Tj
T*(above all, must not criticize it. The)Tj
T*(undemocratic implications of this)Tj
T*(position leave us almost speechless. Are)Tj
T*(elected officials, the members of the)Tj
T*(school board, elected long after and not)Tj
T*(complicit in the illegalities that gave)Tj
T*(rise to the litigation, forbidden, under)Tj
T*(threat of never resuming control of the)Tj
T*(public school system that they were)Tj
T*(elected to govern, to criticize a decree)Tj
T*(that in pursuit of an ambitious and)Tj
T*(possibly quixotic scheme of social)Tj
T*(engineering has imposed a formidable tax)Tj
T*(burden on the people who elected these)Tj
T*(officials?)Tj
